-15","type":"25 PARKING COMPLAINT","outcome":"Parking complaints","recorded_address":"347 E Broad St","recorded_pin":"20014 19059","side":"direct"},{"number":"24082086955","date":"2024-03-22","type":"25 PARKING COMPLAINT","outcome":"Parking complaints","recorded_address":"347 E Broad St","recorded_pin":"20014 19059","side":"direct"},{"number":"24103107864","date":"2024-04-12","type":"25 PARKING COMPLAINT","outcome":"Parking complaints","recorded_address":"347 E Broad St","recorded_pin":"20014 19059","side":"direct"},{"number":"24116122382","date":"2024-04-25","type":"25 PARKING COMPLAINT","outcome":"Parking complaints","recorded_address":"347 E Broad St","recorded_pin":"20014 19059","side":"direct"},{"number":"24121127282","date":"2024-04-30","type":"27 VERBAL DISTURB.","outcome":"Disturbance / nuisance","recorded_address":"347 E Broad St","recorded_pin":"20014 19059","side":"direct"},{"number":"25154156005","date":"2025-06-03","type":"70 PROPERTY/VACATION CHECK","outcome":"Other","recorded_address":"546 E Charlton Ln","recorded_pin":"20014 19056","side":"neighbors"}],"listings":[{"listing_id":"22447750","title":"Historic + Renovated w/ Parking by Lucky Savannah","url":"https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22447750","guests":6.0,"permits":["SVR-02577"],"analysis":{"listing_id":"22447750","signature":"c41e7bfe66511426b9668fb76bb28d71a4050df7940ce3d54627429b2874e490","source_sha256":"66af9ad59cb28609463135148df21b6785a578cbdec2332f47cb0062613e451d","chunks":7,"words":602,"party_signal":0,"social_signal":0.008196007460355759,"party_welcome":0.003084516152739525,"social_amenities":0.015217791311442852,"party_restriction":0.002983817597851157,"nearby_nightlife":0.9363569021224976,"signal_evidence":[],"social_evidence":[{"text":"A door in the dining room leads to a private deck, the perfect quiet spot to enjoy a cup of coffee as you start you day. Inside, just off of the dining room is the elevated kitchen, which features an ample amount of counter space and everything you need to enjoy an evening in. The home's half bath is neatly tucked away under the staircase. At the top of the stairs you\u2019ll find the laundry room and a subway tile shower/tub combination, with a large vanity, that boasts with light. Each bedroom features a king size bed, large smart television, and plenty of storage for your belongings.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":43,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00013039475015830249,"social_amenities":0.008196007460355759,"party_restriction":0.0005101874121464789,"nearby_nightlife":0.018531041219830513}},{"text":"Historic charm abounds in this 2 bedroom, 2.5 bath home. With a living room with sleeper sofa, separate dining room, and huge kitchen with tons of light you'll feel right at home for your stay in Savannah. The space This beautiful home is only minutes away from historic River Street, bustling Broughton Street, and within steps to Mother Mathilda Beasly Dog Park. With a living room with sleeper sofa, separate dining room, and spacious light-filled kitchen, you'll feel right at home for your stay in Savannah. The parlor, which opens to the dining room, will be to your left when you enter the foyer.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":38,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.000177634836290963,"social_amenities":0.004890591371804476,"party_restriction":0.0005817477940581739,"nearby_nightlife":0.019105004146695137}}],"evidence":{"party_welcome":[{"text":"The main bedroom, facing the front of the home overlooking the tree-lined streets, additionally features a bright and airy ensuite bathroom with walk-in shower. In the morning, stroll down the cobblestones of Jones Street, dubbed \u201cAmerica\u2019s prettiest street\u201d by Southern Living Magazine, for breakfast at Clary\u2019s Cafe, the setting for several breakfast scenes in Midnight in the Garden of Good and Evil. From there, you\u2019ll be steps away from the Cathedral of St. John the Baptist, which underwent a major restoration to preserve their beautiful stained glass windows and architectural integrity. What is parking like for this home? Non-metered Parking","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":45,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.003084516152739525,"social_amenities":0.015217791311442852,"party_restriction":0.0027958841528743505,"nearby_nightlife":0.9363569021224976}},{"text":"What this place offers Bathroom Hair dryer Shampoo Conditioner Body soap Hot water Shower gel Bedroom and laundry Washer Dryer Essentials Towels, bed sheets, soap, and toilet paper Hangers Bed linens Iron Entertainment TV with standard cable Heating and cooling Air conditioning Heating Home safety Smoke alarm Carbon monoxide alarm Fire extinguisher Internet and office Wifi Dedicated workspace Kitchen and dining Kitchen Space where guests can cook their own meals Refrigerator Microwave Dishes and silverware Plates, bowls, cups, cutlery, and other utensils Dishwasher Stove Oven Coffee maker Toaster Coffee Location features Private entrance Separate street or building entrance Services Pets allowed Assistance animals are always allowed Long term stays allowed","section":"AMENITIES","line":67,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00046241949894465506,"social_amenities":0.0015390949556604028,"party_restriction":0.0003949602833017707,"nearby_nightlife":0.0006926235510036349}}],"social_amenities":[{"text":"The main bedroom, facing the front of the home overlooking the tree-lined streets, additionally features a bright and airy ensuite bathroom with walk-in shower. In the morning, stroll down the cobblestones of Jones Street, dubbed \u201cAmerica\u2019s prettiest street\u201d by Southern Living Magazine, for breakfast at Clary\u2019s Cafe, the setting for several breakfast scenes in Midnight in the Garden of Good and Evil. From there, you\u2019ll be steps away from the Cathedral of St. John the Baptist, which underwent a major restoration to preserve their beautiful stained glass windows and architectural integrity. What is parking like for this home? Non-metered Parking","sectio