of our cozier Savannah vacation rentals with a great location overlooking Orleans Square, is a garden level property with the same name.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":38,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.048249658197164536,"social_amenities":0.10139148682355881,"party_restriction":0.002651011571288109,"nearby_nightlife":0.03448973223567009}}],"nearby_nightlife":[{"text":"- Soho South Cafe - The Public Kitchen and Bar Orleans Square is uniquely located close to a number of Savannah College of Art and Design (SCAD) facilities, and next door to the location of SCAD\u2019s graduation ceremonies. Whether you are visiting SCAD, moving your child in or out of one of SCAD\u2019s dormitories, attending parents weekend, or attending SCAD graduation, Orleans Square is in an ideal location, and can accommodate you and your family comfortably. Just north of this property are sites such as Oglethorpe House, the Telfair Museums, Jepson Center for the Arts and the Museum Store for both.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":57,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.6734334230422974,"social_amenities":0.004558817483484745,"party_restriction":0.0012602823553606868,"nearby_nightlife":0.9880790114402771}},{"text":"The north end beach even offers the opportunity to get a bit of both as you can watch maritime traffic come from the ocean into the Port of Savannah, which is one of the busiest ports in the country. When you stay in Savannah Georgia vacation homes, you may also have the opportunity to enjoy the special events and celebrations that happen throughout the year in Savannah and on Tybee Island. We can always provide you with an updated list, but the following are some examples: \u2022 Annual Martin Luther King, Jr. Day Celebration in January \u2022 Savannah Irish Festival in February \u2022 Mardi Gras Tybee in February","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":85,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.6990110278129578,"social_amenities":0.003015604568645358,"party_restriction":0.0009524585912004113,"nearby