l electric stove Oven Hot water kettle Coffee maker: pour-over coffee Wine glasses Toaster Baking sheet Dining table Coffee Location features Private entrance Separate street or building entrance Outdoor Shared patio or balcony Shared backyard \u2013 Fully fenced An open space on the property usually covered in grass Outdoor furniture Outdoor dining area Parking and facilities","section":"AMENITIES","line":103,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0005900447140447795,"social_amenities":0.1890040785074234,"party_restriction":0.0008668668451718986,"nearby_nightlife":0.0012556471629068255}},{"text":"Charming carriage house in a historic home built in 1850 with a beautiful courtyard garden. Located in the design district with the most stylish and chic boutiques just around the corner. Walk to the park, stores and restaurants. Peaceful and quiet. Renovated and furnished by the owner, a local interior designer. Renovated bathroom and kitchen. Parking is on street. Read details in the parking section before asking. No pets. ANY 3rd occupant must be disclosed at inquiry. SVR-02205 The space Ground level of a Charming Carriage House. Original hardwood floors and exposed brick give it the Savannah Historic feel.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":42,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00021018908591941,"social_amenities":0.01617990992963314,"party_restriction":0.9688606858253479,"nearby_nightlife":0.8923789262771606}}],"party_restriction":[{"text":"Charming carriage house in a historic home built in 1850 with a beautiful courtyard garden. Located in the design district with the most stylish and chic boutiques just around the corner. Walk to the park, stores and restaurants. Peaceful and quiet. Renovated and furnished by the owner, a local interior designer. Renovated bathroom and kitchen. Parking is on street. Read details in the parking section before asking. No pets. ANY 3rd occupant must be disclosed at inquiry. SVR-02205 The space Ground level of a Charming Carriage House. Original hardwood floors and exposed brick give it the Savannah Historic feel.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":42,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00021018908591941,"social_amenities":0.01617990992963314,"party_restriction":0.9688606858253479,"nearby_nightlife":0.8923789262771606}},{"text":"If you don't want to worry about meters get a visitor's parking pass at the visitor's center just 5 min walk from the apartment **CLOSED DUE TO COVID**. It costs $15 per day, they will give it to you for as many days as you want. Put it on your dashboard and don't have to feed any meter. DURING COVID: Get passes at the Parking and Mobility Office on Bryan Street also downtown just a few minutes away. You have to call ahead, airbnb won't let me disclose website or number here but just search \"Savannah Parking and Mobility\" and got to \"Visitor\" tab, it's all clear there.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":59,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00016129676077980548,"social_amenities":0.0018061615992337465,"party_restriction":0.0033189463429152966,"nearby_nightlife":0.0007109782891348004}}],"nearby_nightlife":[{"text":"Charming carriage house in a historic home built in 1850 with a beautiful courtyard garden. Located in the design district with the most stylish and chic boutiques just around the corner. Walk to the park, stores and restaurants. Peaceful and quiet. Renovated and furnished by the owner, a local interior designer. Renovated bathroom and kitchen. Parking is on street. Read details in the parking section before asking. No pets. ANY 3rd occupant must be disclosed at inquiry. SVR-02205 The space Ground level of a Charming Carriage House. Original hardwood floors and exposed brick give it the Savannah Historic feel.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":42,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00021018908591941,"social_amenities":0.01617990992963314,"party_restriction":0.9688606858253479,"nearby_nightlife":0.8923789262771606}},{"text":"What this place offers Scenic views Courtyard view Garden view Bat