"party_restriction":[{"text":"OCCUPANCY: We NEVER allow more than 2 people, including infants/children, at the property at ANY/ALL times. NO PARTIES ALLOWED! NO BACHELORETTE/BACHOLOR GROUPS! No pets or smoking allowed. PARKING INFO: There is no parking at the home. This is located on a LANE/alley so the closet street parking is one block in any direction. 1. Luxury Living Savannah has 4 privately reserved parking spaces (a few blocks away) that are available to our guests for rent. We charge $20 per night, per space and this can be added to your reservation charges. Please arrange for this at time of booking and provide vehicle tag number & state.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":70,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0003437624254729599,"social_amenities":0.0004716751864179969,"party_restriction":0.9983888864517212,"nearby_nightlife":0.9438225626945496}},{"text":"We charge $20 per day, per space and this will be added to your reservation charges. Please arrange for this at time of booking and provide vehicle tag number & state. 2. This property (and all downtown Savannah) has metered, on-street parking Monday through Friday, free on Saturday/Sunday. The City of Savannah uses Meter Pay Stations or coin meters. You can download the APP \"Park Savannah\" for easy payments from your phone. Visitor Parking Passes are available for 24hours/$15.00 and 48hours/$24.00. Passes are available at the City of Savannah Parking Services Office (100 East Bryan Street) from 8am - 5pm.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":93,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00025854521663859487,"social_amenities":0.000965844199527055,"party_restriction":0.0034643535036593676,"nearby_nightlife":0.022793931886553764}}],"nearby_nightlife":[{"text":"Great for sunny lunches and evening cocktails. In the courtyard is a small shed with a washer and dryer that are for your use but also shared with guests in the next door cottage. Nearby attractions include The Sorrel-Weed House, Green-Meldrim House, Mercer Williams H