 arrives, enjoy handcrafted cocktails at Artillery Bar, rooftop views at Peregrin, or a lively atmosphere at McDonough's before returning to your peaceful retreat. Savannah offers unforgettable experiences throughout the year. Spring welcomes blooming gardens, the internationally known St. Patrick's Day celebration, and the Savannah Music Festival. Summer brings outdoor dining, riverfront evenings, and Fourth of July festivities. Autumn features the Savannah Jazz Festival and SCAD Film Festival, while winter transforms the city with Savannah Holly Days, the River Street Christmas Market, and the beloved Lighted Boat Parade.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":69,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.9717312455177307,"social_amenities":0.041969768702983856,"party_restriction":0.0034928550012409687,"nearby_nightlife":0.9961051940917969}},{"text":"Day before Thanksgiving, Thanksgiving Day, and the day after Thanksgiving Day before Christmas Eve, Christmas Eve & Day, and the day after Christmas Day Day before New Years Day, New Years Day, and the day after New Years Day Day before MLK Day, MLK Day, and the day after MLK Day Summer Hours of the North End Pool - Unheated Open daily from 10:00 a.m.\u20135:00 p.m. May 31\u2013Tuesday after Labor Day Guests with Pets This property happily welcomes your furry travel companions! Guests may bring up to 2 dogs, with a combined weight limit of 50 lbs.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":119,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0006315690698102117,"social_amenities":0.019241690635681152,"party_restriction":0.0003735982463695109,"nearby_nightlife":0.0034855869598686695}}],"social_amenities":[{"text":"Our guests have access to our beautiful, heated pool that is located on the South End of Tybee Island. For our Savannah properties, it is a scenic 25-minute drive through Wilmington and Whitemarsh Island, taking you over the Savannah River Delta onto Tybee Island. The Pool is open during the below dates and times. March 1 - Oct 31: Open 7 days a week from 10am-5pm. Nov 1 - Feb 28/29: Open Friday and Saturday from 10am-5pm Additional Pool Hours available during the off-season are listed below. If these dates fall in the middle of the week, the pool will be open as listed below and every Friday and Saturday.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":105,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00018984753114636987,"social_amenities":0.8883350491523743,"party_restriction":0.002244511852040887,"nearby_nightlife":0.0010255929082632065}},{"text":"Hot water kettle Coffee maker Wine glasses Toaster Blender Dining table Location features Private entrance Separate street or building entrance Outdoor Patio or balcony Outdoor furniture Parking and facilities Free parking on premises Pool Services Pets allowed Assistance animals are always allowed Self check-in Keypad Check yourself into the home with a door code Not included Unavailable: Washer Washer","section":"AMENITIES","line":191,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0003897888818755746,"social_amenities":0.06806761026382446,"party_restriction":0.0021952958777546883,"nearby_nightlife":0.0005317201721481979}}],"party_restriction":[{"text":"History lovers will appreciate being just five minutes from the Telfair Museum and only a short stroll from the Green-Meldrim House, the Sorrel-Weed House Museum, and many of Savannah's beautifully preserved historic landmarks. Nearby Pulaski Square provides one of the city's most picturesque settings for leisurely walks beneath towering live oaks draped with Spanish moss. Dining options surround the neighborhood. Enjoy Southern favorites at Mrs. Wilkes' Dining Room, gather for dinner at The Public Kitchen, or experience one of Savannah's oldest restaurants at Crystal Beer Parlor.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":69,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0002993810921907425,"social_amenities":0.0029563535936176777,"party_restriction":0.003978117369115353,"nearby_nightlife":0.9622676968574524}},{"text":"As evening arrives, enjoy handcrafted cocktails at Artillery Bar, rooftop views at Peregrin, or a lively atmosphere at McDonough's before returning to your peaceful retreat. Savannah offers unforgettable experiences throughout the year. Spring welcomes blooming gardens, the internationally known St. Patrick's Day celebration, and the Savannah Music Festival. Summer brings outdoor dining, riverfront evenings, and Fourth of July festivities. Autumn features the Savannah Jazz Festival and SCAD Film Festival, while winter transforms the city with Savannah Holly Days, the River Street Christmas Market, and the beloved Lighted Boat Parade.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":69,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.9717312455177307,"social_amenities":0.041969768702983856,"party_restriction":0.0034928550012409687,"nearby_nightlife":0.9961051940917969}}],"nearby_nightlife":[{"text":"As evening arrives, enjoy handcrafted cocktails at Artillery Bar, rooftop views at Peregrin, or a lively atmosphere at McDonough's before returning to your peaceful retreat. Savannah offers unforgettable experiences throughout the year. Spring welcomes blooming gardens, the internationally known St. Patrick's Day celebration, and the Savannah Music Festival. Summer brings outdoor dining, riverfront evenings, and Fourth of July festivities. Autumn features the Savannah Jazz Festival and SCAD Film Festival, while winter transforms the city with Savannah Holly Days, the River Street Christmas Market, and the beloved Lighted Boat Parade.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":69,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.9717312455177307,"social_amenities":0.041969768702983856,"party_restriction":0.0034928550012409687,"nearby_nightlife":0.9961051940917969}},{"text":"Start each morning with a fresh cup of coffee from Savannah Coffee Roasters next door before setting off to explore Savannah on foot. Spend your days wandering picturesque squares, browsing local boutiques, touring historic homes, or lingering over long lunches before returning to your comfortable home away from home. Forsyth Park is approximately ten minutes away on foot, offering beautiful gardens, the famous fountain, shaded walking paths, and the popular Saturday farmers market. Walk about ten minutes to Broughton Street to discover local boutiques, galleries, and shopping, or continue fifteen minutes to River Street, where historic cobblestone streets meet waterfront restaurants, entertainment, and scenic river views.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":61,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00020086392760276794,"social_amenities":0.0023304361384361982,"party_restriction":0.0009173061116598547,"nearby_nightlife":0.9733008146286011}}]}}}],"complete":true},{"pin":"20031 16019","address":"201 W LIBERTY ST","permit_type":"non_owner","approved_guests":4.0,"advertised_guests":2.0,"neighbor_count":2,"counts":{"direct":{"All calls":0,"Noise-party-disturbance":0,"Parking complaints":0,"Noise complaints":0,"Loud party":0,"Disturbance / nuisance":0},"neighbors":{"All calls":0,"Noise-party-disturbance":0,"Parking complaints":0,"Noise complaints":0,"Loud party":0,"Disturbance / nuisance":0},"combined":{"All calls":0,"Noise-party-disturbance":0,"Parking complaints":0,"Noise complaints":0,"Loud party":0,"Disturbance / nuisance":0}},"calls":[],"listings":[{"listing_id":"22447596","title":"Bird Baldwin House, Parking by Lucky Savannah","url":"https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/22447596","guests":2.0,"permits":["SVR-00613"],"analysis":{"listing_id":"22447596","signature":"c41e7bfe66511426b9668fb76bb28d71a4050df7940ce3d54627429b2874e490","source_sha256":"24897b64475c9b9d33b190d500bbe9ab9c06215f465180037e11c897668718fa","chunks":7,"words":638,"party_signal":0,"social_signal":0.009188196621835232,"party_welcome":0.0032290187664330006,"social_amenities":0.01710660755634308,"party_restriction":0.011007999069988728,"nearby_nightlife":0.9328809380531311,"signal_evidence":[],"social_evidence":[{"text":"Great Location and a reserved off-street parking space. This Savannah condo offers soaring ceilings and Savannah heart pine flooring. Large windows offer a great view and lots of light but also privacy since the unit is on the third floor. The space Why Lucky Savannah Loves this Property: - Situated on the third floor of this historic home, you\u2019ll have lots of light, privacy, and a shared balcony. - Located directly across from the Savannah Civic Center, site of SCAD graduations, this home is perfect for visiting SCAD parents! - You\u2019ll have one complimentary parking spot located in the rear of this vacation home.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":38,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0032290187664330006,"social_amenities":0.009188196621835232,"party_restriction":0.004169994965195656,"nearby_nightlife":0.05123328045010567}},{"text":"The Bird-Baldwin House survived many subsequent transformations, including time as a boarding house and tavern known as \u201cHarry\u2019s Place,\u201d before finally being restored and renovated. This Savannah condo offers soaring ceilings, Savannah heart pine flooring, and large windows. The galley kitchen has everything you need to enjoy a meal, or to warm up any leftovers from Savannah\u2019s extensive selection of restaurants. Fully equipped with all of the modern conveniences one could ask for; Convection oven/microwave, dishwasher, refrigerator, dishes & utensils and a coffee maker. Enjoy a morning cup of joe on the back porch, or a evening glass of wine after a long day of sightseeing.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":49,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00045221438631415367,"social_amenities":0.0027165752835571766,"party_restriction":0.0006100818864069879,"nearby_nightlife":0.27176693081855774}}],"evidence":{"party_welcome":[{"text":"Great Location and a reserved off-street parking space. This Savannah condo offers soaring ceilings and Savannah heart pine flooring. Large windows offer a great view and lots of light but also privacy since the unit is on the third floor. The space Why Lucky Savannah Loves this Property: - Situated on the third floor of this historic home, you\u2019ll have lots of light, privacy, and a shared balcony. - Located directly across from the Savannah Civic Center, site of SCAD graduations, this home is perfect for visiting SCAD parents! - You\u2019ll have one complimentary parking spot located in the rear of this vacation home.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":38,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0032290187664330006,"social_amenities":0.009188196621835232,"party_restriction":0.004169994965195656,"nearby_nightlife":0.05123328045010567}},{"text":"The Bird-Baldwin House survived many subsequent transformations, including time as a boarding house and tavern known as \u201cHarry\u2019s Place,\u201d before finally being restored and renovated. This Savannah condo offers soaring ceilings, Savannah heart pine flooring, and large windows. The galley kitchen has everything you need to enjoy a meal, or to warm up any leftovers from Savannah\u2019s extensive selection of restaurants. Fully equipped with all of the modern conveniences one could ask for; Convection oven/microwave, dishwasher, refrigerator, dishes & utensils and a coffee maker. Enjoy a morning cup of joe on the back porch, or a evening glass of wine after a long day of sightseeing.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":49,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00045221438631415367,"social_amenities":0.0027165752835571766,"party_restriction":0.0006100818864069879,"nearby_nightlife":0.27176693081855774}}],"social_amenities":[{"text":"You\u2019ll be a short walk from the Savannah Visitor\u2019s Center, where you can easily pick up a guided trolley tour. While you\u2019re out, have lunch at Soho South Cafe. Dishes like their Seared Salmon BLT (with spinach, tomato, bacon, and a tangy garlic aioli on a toasted honey wheat roll ) and Howlin\u2019 Chicken (fried chicken breast with fried pickles, cheddar cheese, and house made jalapeno ranch) will make you glad you did! Parking: Private Parking This unit includes a private parking space located at the rear of the property. Additional vehicles will need to be park on the street, which may be metered or non-metered.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":53,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0002660044701769948,"social_amenities":0.01710660755634308,"party_restriction":0.004809736739844084,"nearby_nightlife":0.9328809380531311}},{"text":"Great Location and a reserved off-street parking space. This Savannah condo offers soaring ceilings and Savannah heart pine flooring. Large windows offer a great view and lots of light but also privacy since the unit is on the third floor. The space Why Lucky Savannah Loves this Property: - Situated on the third floor of this historic home, you\u2019ll have lots of light, privacy, and a shared balcony. - Located directly across from the Savannah Civic Center, site of SCAD graduations, this home is perfect for visiting SCAD parents! - You\u2019ll have one complimentary parking spot located in the rear of this vacation home.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":38,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0032290187664330006,"social_amenities":0.009188196621835232,"party_restriction":0.004169994965195656,"nearby_nightlife":0.05123328045010567}}],"party_restriction":[{"text":"The Bird-Baldwin House has a rich, southern history. Built by Lewis Bird in 1838, it is the oldest home in Savannah South of Liberty Street. Bird, a prominent Savannah attorney, began the construct but tragically perished with his entire family on the Steamboat Pulaski when it exploded and sank off the coast of North Carolina on June 14, 1838. Bird's mother completed the house and sold it to his law partner, Mr. Baldwin, who lived in it for many years. The house was commandeered and occupied by General Sherman\u2019s staff as a temporary headquarters in December 1864, after Sherman\u2019s infamous March to the Sea.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":47,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00042870116885751486,"social_amenities":0.0009162526694126427,"party_restriction":0.011007999069988728,"nearby_nightlife":0.01405632309615612}},{"text":"You\u2019ll be a short walk from the Savannah Visitor\u2019s Center, where you can easily pick up a guided trolley tour. While you\u2019re out, have lunch at Soho South Cafe. Dishes like their Seared Salmon BLT (with spinach, tomato, bacon, and a tangy garlic aioli on a toasted honey wheat roll ) and Howlin\u2019 Chicken (fried chicken breast with fried pickles, cheddar cheese, and house made jalapeno ranch) will make you glad you did! Parking: Private Parking This unit includes a private parking space located at the rear of the property. Additional vehicles will need to be park on the street, which may be metered or non-metered.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":53,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0002660044701769948,"social_amenities":0.01710660755634308,"party_restriction":0.004809736739844084,"nearby_nightlife":0.9328809380531311}}],"nearby_nightlife":[{"text":"You\u2019ll be a short walk from the Savannah Visitor\u2019s Center, where you can easily pick up a guided trolley tour. While you\u2019re out, have lunch at Soho South Cafe. Dishes like their Seared Salmon BLT (with spinach, tomato, bacon, and a tangy garlic aioli on a toasted honey wheat roll ) and Howlin\u2019 Chicken (fried chicken breast with fried pickles, cheddar cheese, and house made jalapeno ranch) will make you glad you did! Parking: Private Parking This unit includes a private parking space located at the rear of the property. Additional vehicles will need to be park on the street, which may be metered or non-metered.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":53,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0002660044701769948,"social_amenities":0.01710660755634308,"party_restriction":0.004809736739844084,"nearby_nightlife":0.9328809380531311}},{"text":"The Bird-Baldwin House survived many subsequent transformations, including time as a boarding house and tavern known as \u201cHarry\u2019s Place,\u201d before finally being restored and renovated. This Savannah condo off