13808687799610198,"social_amenities":0.7083446383476257,"party_restriction":0.0006681765080429614,"nearby_nightlife":0.0013353944523259997}},{"text":"Hot water kettle Coffee maker Wine glasses Toaster Baking sheet Blender Dining table Location features Private entrance Separate street or building entrance Outdoor Patio or balcony Backyard An open space on the property usually covered in grass Outdoor furniture Parking and facilities Pool Paid parking off premises Services Pets allowed Assistance animals are always allowed Long term stays allowed Allow stay for 28 days or more Self check-in Keypad Check yourself into the home with a door code","section":"AMENITIES","line":197,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0007704944000579417,"social_amenities":0.04757565259933472,"party_restriction":0.001487942412495613,"nearby_nightlife":0.0006187316030263901}}],"evidence":{"party_welcome":[{"text":"If these dates fall in the middle of the week, the pool will be open as listed below and every Friday and Saturday. Day before Thanksgiving, Thanksgiving Day, and the day after Thanksgiving Day before Christmas Eve, Christmas Eve & Day, and the day after Christmas Day Day before New Years Day, New Years Day, and the day after New Years Day Day before MLK Day, MLK Day, and the day after MLK Day Summer Hours of the North End Pool - Unheated Open daily from 10:00 a.m.\u20135:00 p.m. May 31\u2013Tuesday after Labor Day Guests with Pets This property happily welcomes your furry travel companions!","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":115,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00875610951334238,"social_amenities":0.02446587383747101,"party_restriction":0.001342608593404293,"nearby_nightlife":0.006124743260443211}},{"text":"Located just blocks from the heart of Savannah downtown, Pickett's Place offers an unmatched mix of convenience, creature comforts and historic charm. This beautiful townhouse is tucked into a quiet corner at the intersection of Jones and Tattnall Streets. It's just blocks from lush, centuries-old Chatham and Pulaski Squares, resplendent outdoor spaces in which meandering tourists often come face-to-face with wedding parties, historical reenactments and performance artists. What's more, Pickett's Place is close to some of Savannah's finest cultural and culinary establishments. When you're this close to the center of the Savannah GA Historic District, anything seems possible. Other Savannah Vacation Rentals Can't Match These Charms","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":45,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.002558257197961211,"social_amenities":0.12373925000429153,"party_restriction":0.0007124929106794298,"nearby_nightlife":0.8523232340812683}}],"social_amenities":[{"text":"Other things to note Heated Pool Access Our guests have access to our beautiful, heated pool that is located on the South End of Tybee Island. For our Savannah properties, it is a scenic 25-minute drive through Wilmington and Whitemarsh Island, taking you over the Savannah River Delta onto Tybee Island. The Pool is open during the below dates and times. March 1 - Oct 31: Open 7 days a week from 10am-5pm. Nov 1 - Feb 28/29: Open Friday and Saturday from 10am-5pm Additional Pool Hours available during the off-season are listed below.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":102,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00013808687799610198,"social_amenities":0.7083446383476257,"party_restriction":0.0006681765080429614,"nearby_nightlife":0.0013353944523259997}},{"text":"Located just blocks from the heart of Savannah downtown, Pickett's Place offers an unmatched mix of convenience, creature comforts and historic charm. This beautiful townhouse is tucked into a quiet corner at the intersection of Jones and Tattnall Streets. It's just blocks from lush, centuries-old Chatham and Pulaski Squares, resplendent outdoor spaces in which meandering tourists often come face-to-face with wedding parties, historical reenactments and performance artists. What's more, Pickett's Place is close to some of Savannah's finest cultural and culinary establishments. When you're this close to the center of the Savannah GA Historic District, anything seems possible. Other Savannah Vacation Rentals Can't Match These Charms","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":45,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.002558257197961211,"social_amenities":0.12373925000429153,"party_restriction":0.0007124929106794298,"nearby_nightlife":0.8523232340812683}}],"party_restriction":[{"text":"Whether it's central heating and cooling to get you through Savannah's unpredictable nights, a powerful washer-dryer that eliminates the need to find a laundromat or full-house wifi that ensures you remain connected to those who couldn't be with you on your trip, this property leaves other Savannah vacation rentals in the dust. Things to Do in Savannah Downtown The bustling, cobbled streets and sidewalks of Savannah downtown truly offer something for everyone. If you're looking for a cultural experience to rival anything you'd find in Atlanta or New York, visit the art exhibits at the nearby Telfair Museum or Jepson Art Gallery.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":61,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00095987762324512,"social_amenities":0.05840473622083664,"party_restriction":0.009017539210617542,"nearby_nightlife":0.9290261268615723}},{"text":"For a more contemporary take on visual art, the Julia Christian Gallery and the Savannah College of Art and Design's galleries sit within easy walking distance. To discover pieces of colonial history that you may have thought were lost to the mists of time forever, visit the Davenport House Museum, Georgia Historical Society or Georgia Railroad Museum. If you wouldn't pass up a shopping opportunity for the world, never fear: The world-renowned shops and stores of Broughton Street aren't far off. Make Your Mark at Pickett's Place Today","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":69,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0008838109788484871,"social_amenities":0.0033536572009325027,"party_restriction":0.0024988616351038218,"nearby_nightlife":0.7122565507888794}}],"nearby_nightlife":[{"text":"Whether it's central heating and cooling to get you through Savannah's unpredictable nights, a powerful washer-dryer that eliminates the need to find a laundromat or full-house wifi that ensures you remain connected to those who couldn't be with you on your trip, this property leaves other Savannah vacation rentals in the dust. Things to Do in Savannah Downtown The bustling, cobbled streets and sidewalks of Savannah downtown truly offer something for everyone. If you're looking for a cultural experience to rival anything you'd find in Atlanta or New York, visit the art exhibits at the nearby Telfair Museum or Jepson Art Gallery.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":61,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00095987762324512,"social_amenities":0.05840473622083664,"party_restriction":0.009017539210617542,"nearby_nightlife":0.9290261268615723}},{"text":"Located just blocks from the heart of Savannah downtown, Pickett's Place offers an unmatched mix of convenience, creature comforts and historic charm. This beautiful townhouse is tucked into a quiet corner at the intersection of Jones and Tattnall Streets. It's just blocks from lush, centuries-old Chatham and Pulaski Squares, resplendent outdoor spaces in which meandering tourists often come face-to-face with wedding parties, historical reenactments and performance artists. What's more, Pickett's Place is close to some of Savannah's finest cultural and culinary establishments. When you're this close to the center of the Savannah GA Historic District, anything seems possible. Other Savannah Vacation Rentals Can't Match These Charms","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":45,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.002558257197961211,"social_amenities":0.12373925000429153,"party_restriction":0.0007124929106794298,"nearby_nightlife":0.8523232340812683}}]}}}],"complete":true},{"pin":"20032 06006","address":"16 E JONES ST","permit_type":"non_owner","approved_guests":8.0,"advertised_guests