io space. Enjoy the evenings sipping a glass of wine, or a morning cup of joe on the back porch!","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":45,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0009740364039316773,"social_amenities":0.06849151849746704,"party_restriction":0.00039309205021709204,"nearby_nightlife":0.6246849298477173}}],"party_restriction":[{"text":"Just on the opposite side of the fence, you will find a private parking space designated to your home. Just a short walking distance to the heart of downtown, this property is ideal for travelers looking to stay in a tree-lined, quieter residential part of town without sacrificing convenience. Head West and dine at some of the city's best restaurants, like 700 Drayton, Fox & Fig, and Hitch. Due North toward River Street, guests can shop til they drop inside various local retailers, like The Paris Market & Brocante, 24e, and shopSCAD to name a few.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":49,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00021736569760832936,"social_amenities":0.004736213944852352,"party_restriction":0.002781602321192622,"nearby_nightlife":0.9561656713485718}},{"text":"Situated on East Taylor Street, this charming abode built in 1862 has been tastefully restored, and is the perfect Savannah hideaway. The space This historic home offers all of the amenities one could hope for while staying an extended period of time. Located in the quieter, residential area of the Downtown Historic District, you are surrounded by tree-line views. Situated on East Taylor Street, this charming abode built in 1862 has been tastefully restored, and is the perfect Savannah hideaway.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":38,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00028271411429159343,"social_amenities":0.07816697657108307,"party_restriction":0.0023515329230576754,"nearby_nightlife":0.008126442320644855}}],"nearby_nightlife":[{"text":"Just on the opposite side of the fence, you will find a private parking space designated to your home. Just a short walking distance to the heart 