ers and local favorites. A visit to Savannah would hardly be complete without stopping at Forsyth Park. Not only will you see the famous iron fountain landmark found in \"Midnight in the Garden of Good and Evil,\" but it is also a great place to walk, take children or spend a quiet afternoon with a picnic. Savannah is also the place for ghost hunters with plenty of old cemeteries and ghost tours to enjoy.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":49,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00030324445106089115,"social_amenities":0.001750448253005743,"party_restriction":0.00409851036965847,"nearby_nightlife":0.8432719707489014}}],"nearby_nightlife":[{"text":"Make your way to Monterey Square and The Mercer House, which was built in 1860 and a big part of the well-known film and book \"Midnight in the Garden of Good and Evil.\" Part of the movie was filmed at the house and the Mercer-Williams House Museum is available to tour. River Street is another famous part of historic Savannah and it used to be the center of trade back in the late 1800s. Old cotton warehouses are now a vibrant community of restaurants, shops and bars.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":49,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00042320560896769166,"social_amenities":0.0009783547138795257,"party_restriction":0.0007355486159212887,"nearby_nightlife":0.9875656962394714}},{"text":"Visit the Colonial Cemetery in the heart of downtown and explore six acres of old memorials. There's also a number of events and celebrations that go on in Savannah every year. Make sure to ask what events might be taking place during your stay. The following is just a sample of the possibilities: \u2022 Annual Martin Luther King, Jr. Day Celebration in January \u2022 St. Patrick's Day Celebration in March \u2022 Tybee Island Beach Bum Parade in May \u2022 Fourth of July on the Waterfront in July \u2022 Savannah Jazz Festival in September \u2022 Holiday Tour of Homes in December \u2022 Rock 'N' Roll Marathon Guest access 2 Bedrooms","section":"FULL D