ksgiving Day, and the day after Thanksgiving Day before Christmas Eve, Christmas Eve & Day, and the day after Christmas Day Day before New Years Day, New Years Day, and the day after New Years Day Day before MLK Day, MLK Day, and the day after MLK Day Summer Hours of the North End Pool - Unheated Open daily from 10:00 a.m.\u20135:00 p.m.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":131,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.004243694711476564,"social_amenities":0.021695459261536598,"party_restriction":0.001978736137971282,"nearby_nightlife":0.002593768062070012}}],"evidence":{"party_welcome":[{"text":"Along with all the things to do in the neighborhood of our vacation homes in Savannah GA, there are also a number of special events that go on every year. Be sure to ask us what might be happening, but the following is a list of possibilities by month: January - Martin Luther King Parade February - Savannah Irish Festival and Black Heritage Festival March - Saint Patrick\u2019s Day in Savannah and Annual Savannah Tour of Homes Gardens April - Savannah Music Festival May - Savannah Scottish Games June - Savannah Asian Festival July - Fireworks on the Beach and Fourth of July on the River","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":57,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.9882529377937317,"social_amenities":0.009695311076939106,"party_restriction":0.0014318573521450162,"nearby_nightlife":0.971493661403656}},{"text":"August - Seafood & Music Festival September - Savannah Jazz Festival October - St. Paul\u2019s Greek Festival and Oktoberfest on the River November - Taste of Savannah December - Holiday Tour of Homes and Christmas on the River You can also check out the First Saturday on the River Festival if you're in Savannah between March and December. SVR-00565 Guest access King Bedroom with Private Bath Queen Bedroom with Shared Attached Bath Sitting room with Sleeping for Four (Two Daybeds with Trundles/4 twin beds) and Shared Attached Bath 3 Baths Living Room with Seating for 10 Dining Table that Seats 10 4 Flat Screen Televisions Washer and Dryer","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":75,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.05179331451654434,"social_amenities":0.0016787026543170214,"party_restriction":0.0005568661144934595,"nearby_nightlife":0.9814429879188538}}],"social_amenities":[{"text":"Cable TV with Hi-Definition Channels and Wi-Fi Off Street Parking for 2 Vehicles with on Street Parking Available Gourmet Kitchen Central Air Conditioning and Heat with Separate Units for Each Level Ceiling Fans throughout Recently Renovated Other things to note Heated Pool Access Our guests have access to our beautiful, heated pool that is located on the South End of Tybee Island. For our Savannah properties, it is a scenic 25-minute drive through Wilmington and Whitemarsh Island, taking you over the Savannah River Delta onto Tybee Island. The Pool is open during the below dates and times. March 1 - Oct 31: Open 7 days a week from 10am-5pm.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":110,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00038360964390449226,"social_amenities":0.05026985704898834,"party_restriction":0.001744424575008452,"nearby_nightlife":0.0084884287789464}},{"text":"Nov 1 - Feb 28/29: Open Friday and Saturday from 10am-5pm Additional Pool Hours available during the off-season are listed below. If these dates fall in the middle of the week, the pool will be open as listed below and every Friday and Saturday. Day before Thanksgiving, Thanksgiving Day, and the day after Thanksgiving Day before Christmas Eve, Christmas Eve & Day, and the day after Christmas Day Day before New Years Day, New Years Day, and the day after New Years Day Day before MLK Day, MLK Day, and the day after MLK Day Summer Hours of the North End Pool - Unheated Open daily from 10:00 a.m.\u20135:00 p.m.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":131,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.004243694711476564,"social_amenities":0.021695459261536598,"party_restriction":0.001978736137971282,"nearby_nightlife":0.002593768062070012}}],"party_restriction":[{"text":"The City Market, River Street, Victorian District and Historic District are Savannah's most popular neighborhoods for sight-seeing and you'll definitely want to visit all of them for a look at historic architecture, as well as a variety of shopping and eating options. For history buffs, Savannah has no shortage of museums either. Some popular ones include the Savannah Visitor Center and History Museum, the Ralph Mark Gilbert Civil Rights Museum, the Ships of the Sea Museum and the Roundhouse Railroad Museum.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":53,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0005443179979920387,"social_amenities":0.0008922410779632628,"party_restriction":0.004501223098486662,"nearby_nightlife":0.19358551502227783}},{"text":"You'll find the famous iron fountain on the main walkway and further in, two war memorials and the Fragrant Garden for the Blind. Getting around Savannah is easy with walkable streets and plenty to see just about everywhere. You can also hop on and off the Chatham Area Transit throughout the Historic District. A great way to maximize your time in the city is to take one of the many organized tours. You can select from tours that fit your interest, such as Civil War or ghost tours, or you can take a fun mode of transportation such as a horse-drawn carriage or an old-fashioned trolley.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":49,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00021372608898673207,"social_amenities":0.0012226863764226437,"party_restriction":0.002444226061925292,"nearby_nightlife":0.5127337574958801}}],"nearby_nightlife":[{"text":"August - Seafood & Music Festival September - Savannah Jazz Festival October - St. Paul\u2019s Greek Festival and Oktoberfest on the River November - Taste of Savannah December - Holiday Tour of Homes and Christmas on the River You can also check out the First Saturday on the River Festival if you're in Savannah between March and December. SVR-00565 Guest access King Bedroom with Private Bath Queen Bedroom with Shared Attached Bath Sitting room with Sleeping for Four (Two Daybeds with Trundles/4 twin beds) and Shared Attached Bath 3 Baths Living Room with Seating for 10 Dining Table that Seats 10 4 Flat Screen Televisions Washer and Dryer","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":75,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.05179331451654434,"social_amenities":0.0016787026543170214,"party_restriction":0.0005568661144934595,"nearby_nightlife":0.9814429879188538}},{"text":"Along with all the things to do in the neighborhood of our vacation homes in Savannah GA, there are also a number of special events that go on every year. Be sure to ask us what might be happening, but the following is a list of possibilities by month: January - Martin Luther King Parade February - Savannah Irish Festival and Black Heritage Festival March - Saint Patrick\u2019s Day in Savannah and Annual Savannah Tour of Homes Gardens April - Savannah Music Festival May - Savannah Scottish Games June - Savannah Asian Festival July - Fireworks on the Beach and Fourth of July on the River","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":57,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.9882529377937317,"social_amenities":0.009695311076939106,"party_restriction":0.0014318573521450162,"nearby_nightlife":0.971493661403656}}]}}},{"listing_id":"28801431","title":"Heated Pool Access | 5*Clean | Flex Cancelation","url":"https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/28801431","guests":4.0,"permits":["SVR-01638"],"analysis":{"listing_id":"28801431","signature":"c41e7bfe66511426b9668fb76bb28d71a4050df7940ce3d54627429b2874e490","source_sha256":"d2710411aad6191c8c99e291b7cdb4f7ea841942807a0c348001a5452aec0b7c","chunks":13,"words":1344,"party_signal":0,"social_signal":0.9276015758514404,"party_welcome":0.9839525818824768,"social_amenities":0.9276015758514404,"party_restriction":0.0810583084821701,"nearby_nightlife":0.989626407623291,"signal_evidence":[],"social_evidence":[{"text":"Book One of the Vacation Rentals Savannah GA Visitors Love It's time to put a special twist on your upcoming trip to Savannah by booking a stay at one of the Savannah vacation rentals everybody always loves to stay at. Change of Place Garden Level is a fun, cozy property that has been completely renovated to provide a modern experience in a timeless city. It features all of the practical amenities you need to feel at home. Don't skip this property if you're looking for one of the vacation rentals experienced Savannah GA visitors highly recommend. SVR-01638 Guest access King Bedroom 1 Bathroom Living Room with pull out sofa bed","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":67,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.017568117007613182,"social_amenities":0.9276015758514404,"party_restriction":0.0810583084821701,"nearby_nightlife":0.0014612504746764898}},{"text":"Change of Place Garden Level is a gorgeous property where you can enjoy the pace of Savannah. This renovated garden property is one of the best Savannah vacation homes due to its location right near famous Forsyth Park. Anyone who has ever spent time in this charming city knows that Forsyth Park is Savannah. Change of Place Garden Level offers 800 square feet of living space. It contains one bedroom and one bathroom. This lovely garden property has been completely renovated to offer a fresh look The space Step Inside One of the Top Savannah Vacation Rentals Near Forsyth Park","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":38,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00022037068265490234,"social_amenities":0.12791959941387177,"party_restriction":0.0008578623528592288,"nearby_nightlife":0.0027846249286085367}}],"evidence":{"party_welcome":[{"text":"The city also hosts many after-dark tours that take visitors through spooky and legendary spots. People staying at Savannah vacation rentals also like to take excursions to Tybee Island to see the lighthouse or visit with dolphins. One of the big reasons why people book Savannah vacation homes is to attend some of the many festivals that take place in the city. In fact, visitors can look forward to amazing festivals and events all year long. Some of the highlights that occur throughout the year include the Savannah Jazz Festival, the Pin Point Seafood Festival, Bacon Fest, the River Street Food Festival and the Savannah Music Festival.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":59,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.9839525818824768,"social_amenities":0.007567028049379587,"party_restriction":0.002829318167641759,"nearby_nightlife":0.9745785593986511}},{"text":"The Savannah Historic District is full of architectural pearls and fun attractions. This will be right in your neighborhood if you're staying at Change of Place Garden Level. You can enjoy beautiful homes, visions of moss climbing along the sidewalks and free trolley service when you tour this area. In addition, attractions like the Sorrel Weed House, Bonaventure Cemetery, the Cathedral of St. John the Baptist, Lafayette Square, Old Fort Jackson, Skidaway Island State Park and the childhood home of Flannery O'Connor will all be close by. Making your way down to River Street for great music, great food and some fanfare is also essential when planning a Savannah holiday.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":59,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.19345612823963165,"social_amenities":0.010596263222396374,"party_restriction":0.0010712908115237951,"nearby_nightlife":0.989626407623291}}],"social_amenities":[{"text":"Book One of the Vacation Rentals Savannah GA Visitors Love It's time to put a special twist on your upcoming trip to Savannah by booking a stay at one of the Savannah vacation rentals everybody always loves to stay at. Change of Place Garden Level is a fun, cozy property that has been completely renovated to provide a modern experience in a timeless city. It features all of the practical amenities you need to feel at home. Don't skip this property if you're looking for one of the vacation rentals experienced Savannah GA visitors highly recommend. SVR-01638 Guest access King Bedroom 1 Bathroom Living Room with pull out sofa bed","section":"FULL DESC