HICLE THEFT","outcome":"Other","recorded_address":"541 E Anderson St","recorded_pin":"20053 21047","side":"neighbors"},{"number":"25319324404","date":"2025-11-15","type":"71 SUSPICIOUS ACTIVITY","outcome":"Other","recorded_address":"541 E Anderson St","recorded_pin":"20053 21047","side":"neighbors"},{"number":"26035032996","date":"2026-02-04","type":"8-J RESD BURGLARY","outcome":"Other","recorded_address":"545 E Anderson St","recorded_pin":"20053 21049","side":"neighbors"},{"number":"26109111571","date":"2026-04-19","type":"42 PAST THEFT","outcome":"Other","recorded_address":"541 E Anderson St","recorded_pin":"20053 21047","side":"neighbors"},{"number":"26110112792","date":"2026-04-20","type":"42 PAST THEFT","outcome":"Other","recorded_address":"541 E Anderson St","recorded_pin":"20053 21047","side":"neighbors"},{"number":"26256265893","date":"2026-09-13","type":"65 LOW OCC suspicious package","outcome":"Other","recorded_address":"545 E Anderson St","recorded_pin":"20053 21049","side":"neighbors"}],"listings":[{"listing_id":"1693042322963849375","title":"Off St Parking, Hot Tub, Luxury + Walkable","url":"https://www.airbnb.com/rooms/1693042322963849375","guests":6.0,"permits":["SVR-03269"],"analysis":{"listing_id":"1693042322963849375","signature":"c41e7bfe66511426b9668fb76bb28d71a4050df7940ce3d54627429b2874e490","source_sha256":"fd2c3338f0642e3afdd3234745808b15ec40d9871efbb39441d14db795a17ac5","chunks":15,"words":1384,"party_signal":0,"social_signal":0.9663782715797424,"party_welcome":0.9928531050682068,"social_amenities":0.9663782715797424,"party_restriction":0.002525137737393379,"nearby_nightlife":0.9971411228179932,"signal_evidence":[],"social_evidence":[{"text":"Internet and office Wifi Dedicated workspace Kitchen and dining Kitchen Space where guests can cook their own meals Refrigerator Microwave Cooking basics Pots and pans, oil, salt and pepper Dishes and silverware Plates, bowls, cups, cutlery, and other utensils Freezer Dishwasher Stove Oven Hot water kettle Coffee maker: drip coffee maker, Keurig coffee machine Toaster Blender Barbecue utensils Grill, charcoal, bamboo skewers/iron skewers, etc. Dining table Coffee Location features Private entrance Separate street or building entrance Laundromat nearby Outdoor Private backyard \u2013 Fully fenced An open space on the property usually covered in grass Fire pit Outdoor furniture Outdoor dining area BBQ grill Sun loungers Parking and facilities","section":"AMENITIES","line":164,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00035088005824945867,"social_amenities":0.9663782715797424,"party_restriction":0.0004587749426718801,"nearby_nightlife":0.0038125375285744667}},{"text":"Completely remodeled in 2017, The Julia Ann balances historic charm with modern comfort. The open floor plan main area has a bright, fully equipped kitchen with a stocked coffee bar (we even have to-go cups for your morning walks), a comfortable living room, and a modern dining area. Upstairs, everyone has room to spread out with two queen bedrooms and a spacious king master suite with a screened balcony. \u2714\ufe0e FREE Private Off-Street Parking \u2192 2 cars (Accessed via the alleyway) \u2714\ufe0e Backyard Hot Tub Under String Lights \u2714\ufe0e Fenced Backyard w/ Fire Pit & Seating \u2714\ufe0e Blackstone Flat-Top Grill \u2714\ufe0e Beach Gear Supplied (Chairs, umbrella, boogie boards)","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":53,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.010219428688287735,"social_amenities":0.9280679821968079,"party_restriction":0.0012228959240019321,"nearby_nightlife":0.13389995694160461}}],"evidence":{"party_welcome":[{"text":"It originally opened in 1753 as an inn for seafarers, and now it's a great historic restaurant with a hearty Southern buffet and local ghost stories. \u2714\ufe0e On Saturday mornings, we highly recommend walking 10 minutes down to the south end of Forsyth Park to check out the Saturday Farmers Market for fresh local food and pastries. \u2714\ufe0e Be sure to take a trolley ride to get your historical bearings of Savannah (we like Old Savannah Tours the best.) \u2714\ufe0e The Spooky Savannah Haunted Pub Crawl is a fun way to experience haunted Savannah and also keep the party going!","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":97,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.9928531050682068,"social_amenities":0.005353463348001242,"party_restriction":0.0004961101221852005,"nearby_nightlife":0.9971411228179932}},{"text":"Our home is located on the border of the South Historic District and the Victorian District. We love the location because you can experience Savannah like a local instead of a tourist, and we are surrounded by places we actually go to all the time. \u26154 min \u2192 Bobbie's Diner: A beautifully restored 1950s diner owned by SCAD. Our son's favorite is the pancakes, and the classic breakfast is amazing. \u26155 min \u2192 PERC Coffee: Our absolute go-to for coffee. We love the lattes and the casual warehouse vibe. \ud83c\udf777 min \u2192 Treylor Park Pizza Party: A fun, retro pizza spot with really unique and creative toppings.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":76,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.9683786630630493,"social_amenities":0.0006757623050361872,"party_restriction":0.0002461863914504647,"nearby_nightlife":0.9959717392921448}}],"social_amenities":[{"text":"Internet and office Wifi Dedicated workspace Kitchen and dining Kitchen Space where guests can cook their own meals Refrigerator Microwave Cooking basics Pots and pans, oil, salt and pepper Dishes and silverware Plates, bowls, cups, cutlery, and other utensils Freezer Dishwasher Stove Oven Hot water kettle Coffee maker: drip coffee maker, Keurig coffee machine Toaster Blender Barbecue utensils Grill, charcoal, bamboo skewers/iron skewers, etc. Dining table Coffee Location features Private entrance Separate street or building entrance Laundromat nearby Outdoor Private backyard \u2013 Fully fenced An open space on the property usually covered in grass Fire pit Outdoor furniture Outdoor dining area BBQ grill Sun loungers Parking and facilities","section":"AMENITIES","line":164,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00035088005824945867,"social_amenities":0.9663782715797424,"party_restriction":0.0004587749426718801,"nearby_nightlife":0.0038125375285744667}},{"text":"Completely remodeled in 2017, The Julia Ann balances historic charm with modern comfort. The open floor plan main area has a bright, fully equipped kitchen with a stocked coffee bar (we even have to-go cups for your morning walks), a comfortable living room, and a modern dining area. Upstairs, everyone has room to spread out with two queen bedrooms and a spacious king master suite with a screened balcony. \u2714\ufe0e FREE Private Off-Street Parking \u2192 2 cars (Accessed via the alleyway) \u2714\ufe0e Backyard Hot Tub Under String Lights \u2714\ufe0e Fenced Backyard w/ Fire Pit & Seating \u2714\ufe0e Blackstone Flat-Top Grill \u2714\ufe0e Beach Gear Supplied (Chairs, umbrella, boogie boards)","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":53,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.010219428688287735,"social_amenities":0.9280679821968079,"party_restriction":0.0012228959240019321,"nearby_nightlife":0.13389995694160461}}],"party_restriction":[{"text":"\u261514 min \u2192 Mat\u00e9 Factor: A unique, multi-level rustic teahouse with a great bakery. We love sitting out on the patio here. \ud83c\udf7718 min \u2192 Saint Bibiana: An elegant spot for handmade Italian pastas and great cocktails in a historic setting. \u261520 min \u2192 Collins Quarter at Forsyth: Perfect for a weekend brunch right inside the park. SIGHTS & CONVENIENCES: \u2714\ufe0e To explore Savannah's classic historic sites, head to the waterfront to stroll down the cobblestones of River Street and watch the massive cargo ships pass by.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":86,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.0039921472780406475,"social_amenities":0.0024078842252492905,"party_restriction":0.002525137737393379,"nearby_nightlife":0.9919469952583313}},{"text":"We haven\u2019t had any issues with train horns at night and typically only hear the train once a day in the morning. Other things to note Short-Term Rental License No: SVR-03269 Show more","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":118,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.00015640503261238337,"social_amenities":0.0007711319485679269,"party_restriction":0.0021793353371322155,"nearby_nightlife":0.020591476932168007}}],"nearby_nightlife":[{"text":"It originally opened in 1753 as an inn for seafarers, and now it's a great historic restaurant with a hearty Southern buffet and local ghost stories. \u2714\ufe0e On Saturday mornings, we highly recommend walking 10 minutes down to the south end of Forsyth Park to check out the Saturday Farmers Market for fresh local food and pastries. \u2714\ufe0e Be sure to take a trolley ride to get your historical bearings of Savannah (we like Old Savannah Tours the best.) \u2714\ufe0e The Spooky Savannah Haunted Pub Crawl is a fun way to experience haunted Savannah and also keep the party going!","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":97,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.9928531050682068,"social_amenities":0.005353463348001242,"party_restriction":0.0004961101221852005,"nearby_nightlife":0.9971411228179932}},{"text":"\u2714\ufe0e While you are downtown, you have to stop by Leopold's Ice Cream on Broughton Street\u2014it is an iconic Savannah staple that has been serving amazing, old-school scoops since 1919! \u2714\ufe0e If you want to try a completely different, artsy part of town, you should definitely check out Starland Yard. It's a vibrant outdoor food truck park with a great bar and live music, and it is super family-friendly. \u2714\ufe0e For a fun dinner option, take a straight, easy trip right up Broad Street to the famous Pirate\u2019s House.","section":"FULL DESCRIPTION","line":93,"scores":{"party_welcome":0.011860920116305351,"social_amenities":0.002175098517909646,"party_restriction":0.0003848715277854353,"nearby_nightlife":0.9968787431716919}}]}}}],"complete":true},{